From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:18:32 +0200
Subject: media: ov5640: Fix the focus zone control

The control config had no ops, so the framework cached writes without
ever calling s_ctrl and nothing reached the firmware. The maximum also
only admitted an x of up to 255 even though the control takes the
point in the frame's own pixels.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
@@ -4021,11 +4021,12 @@ static const struct v4l2_ctrl_ops ov5640_ctrl_ops = {
 };
 
 static const struct v4l2_ctrl_config ov5640_ctrl_focus_zone = {
+	.ops = &ov5640_ctrl_ops,
 	.id = V4L2_CID_OV5640_FOCUS_ZONE,
 	.name = "Focus Zone",
 	.type = V4L2_CTRL_TYPE_INTEGER,
 	.min = 0,
-	.max = 0xffffff,
+	.max = 0x7fffffff,
 	.step = 1,
 	.def = 0,
 };
-- 
Armbian

